## Workflow Complete — Summary

**Input:** 3,591 EU E-PRTR facilities across 32 countries

**Phases completed:**
1. **Price retrieval** — Fetched Eurostat electricity (nrg_pc_205) and gas (nrg_pc_203) prices via API for all countries, all years 2007–2025. Cached in `outputs/cached_data/`.
2. **LCOH calculation** — Processed all 1,759 facilities with heat demand data across three pathways per spec v1.3.1
3. **Verification** — Manual spot-check (< 0.001 EUR/MWh_th error), price outlier detection, checklist

**Results (outputs/):**

| File | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `lcoh_results.csv` | 3,591 rows × 29 columns with full LCOH per facility |
| `assumptions_log.md` | Complete A1–A21 register with sources |
| `price_sources_log.csv` | 3,518 price log entries |
| `price_outliers_log.csv` | 328 flagged YoY outliers (141 from 2022-23 crisis) |
| `verification_report.md` | Full checklist + outstanding issues |
| `method_summary.md` | Human-readable formulas and results |
| `progress.log` | Phase timestamps |

**Key findings:**
- **91% of facilities: natural gas is cheapest** — gas still competitive when electricity prices are moderate
- **8% heat battery cheapest** — almost entirely Sweden and Finland, where electricity (€83–90/MWh) beats gas after EU ETS carbon (€60/tCO2 adds ~€13.5/MWh_th to gas)
- **1% heat pump cheapest** — 19 food/drink (8b) facilities in cheap-electricity countries
- **Avg LCOH:** gas 80.7 | heat pump 79.3 | heat battery 180.3 EUR/MWh_th

